abstract: >-
  An open book of executed Jupyter notebooks, with a small NumPy package, on applied
  and physics-constrained modelling for chemical and materials engineers: atom, mass
  and charge balances as linear constraints, least squares with exact constraints,
  data reconciliation and gross-error detection, monotone regression by the
  pool-adjacent-violators algorithm and by I-splines, Huber and quantile regression,
  preprocessing of spectra, principal component analysis, partial least squares,
  process monitoring, K-means, spectral clustering and Gaussian mixtures, regression
  trees, random forests and gradient boosting, and split conformal prediction
  intervals with out-of-distribution checks. Every method is written out in NumPy and
  checked against an exact result or an independent calculation. All data sets are
  synthetic.
